WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.240 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Attack path analysis follows
individual routes through the

2
00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:04.980 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
FireSat tutorial tree.

3
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:09.240 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
A route ending in an unblocked terminal
Attack is an unresolved residual

4
00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:12.500 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
vulnerability unless its
incoming relationship records

5
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:13.800 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
an allowed disposition.

6
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:18.360 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
This view identifies what remains
possible and its recorded disposition.

7
00:00:18.738 --> 00:00:22.460 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Choose Attack path
analysis, set Status to RV,

8
00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.280 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
and select the Abuse counter rollover route.

9
00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.380 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Follow the highlighted cards
and the Full path list.

10
00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.560 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
The displayed sort metric
comes from the terminal leaf.

11
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.200 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
A single route is not the complete
combination required by an AND scenario.

12
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:39.060 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Open the terminal attack’s
incoming relationship.

13
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.720 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Select Allowed residual vulnerability,

14
00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:45.420 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
enter a specific review rationale
of at least twenty characters,

15
00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:47.620 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
and choose Stage relationship.

16
00:00:48.035 --> 00:00:51.960 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
In this training example, record the
bounded exposure and the further review

17
00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:56.540 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
required; do not imply that writing a
reason establishes external approval.

18
00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:58.860 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Change the filter to ALLOWED.

19
00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:03.840 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
In SSTPA, an Allowed Residual
Vulnerability, or ARV,

20
00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.300 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
carries its associated risk, conditions,

21
00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.380 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
and responsible authority’s decision.

22
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:13.020 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Here the tool records an analyst
disposition on a Loss-scoped relationship.

23
00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:15.120 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Another incoming route can differ.

24
00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:17.600 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
The attack remains technically possible,

25
00:01:17.679 --> 00:01:20.000 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
and its intrinsic metrics are unchanged.

26
00:01:20.263 --> 00:01:24.100 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Contrast Complete block on an
Attack-to-Countermeasure relationship.

27
00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:27.860 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
That flag asserts that the modeled
route cannot succeed under stated

28
00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:30.080 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
conditions and needs supporting evidence.

29
00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:33.560 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
An allowed residual
vulnerability instead supports a

30
00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.280 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
documented acceptance process.

31
00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:37.820 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
The tool records the analyst’s disposition;

32
00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:41.460 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
the responsible authority’s
decision and conditions still need

33
00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:42.380 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
to be established.

34
00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:46.460 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
At the upper right of the canvas,
select Nocturne for dark mode,

35
00:01:46.615 --> 00:01:48.240 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
then Parchment to return.

36
00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:50.500 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
This changes presentation only.
